{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Like almonds.</b> As its Targum renders — they were engraved, in the manner done for silver and gold vessels that are called נייל\"יר בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>Three calyxes.</b> Protruding from each and every branch." "<b>A knob and a flower.</b> There was on each and every branch."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French noelier, 'niello-work/engraved metalwork'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:32.895217195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}